SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 07/19/21: Policy for Remote Participation in 
 Commission Meetings as adopted on 7/19/21 ( link to original hearing notic
 e & Memo ).
DESCRIPTION:Maine Human Rights Commission \n# 51 State House Station\, Aug
 usta\, ME 04333-0051 \n \nPhysical location: 19 Union Street\, Augusta\, M
 E 04330 \nPhone (207) 624-6290   ■    Fax (207) 624-8729  ■   TTY: Mai
 ne Relay 711 \nwww.maine.gov/mhrc \nAmy M. Sneirson                       
   Barbara Archer Hirsch \nEXECUTIVE DIRECTOR COMMISSION COUNSEL \n \n \nME
 MORANDUM \nTo:  Persons attending public meetings of the Maine Human Right
 s Commission   \nFrom:  Amy Sneirson\, Executive Director  \nDate:  July 1
 9\, 2021 \nSubject:           Policy Regarding Remote Participation in Pub
 lic Proceedings of the Maine Human Rights \nCommission \n               \n
 Having given notice to the public of the intent of the Maine Human Rights 
 Commission (“Commission”) to \nadopt a policy governing remote partici
 pation in public Commission meetings\, and having held a hearing \nregardi
 ng the same\, as of this date the Commission adopted this Policy to govern
  remote methods of \nparticipation in public Commission proceedings. This 
 Policy is effective immediately. \nA. As set forth in the Maine Freedom of
  Access Act\, 1 Maine Revised Statutes §403-B\, the Commission \nmay allo
 w or require members of the Commission (“Commissioners”) or the public
  (“Public”) to \nattend or participate public Commission proceedings v
 ia remote methods as set forth below.  \n \nB. “Remote methods"\, define
 d in 1 M.R.S. §403-B (1)\, means telephonic or video technology allowing 
 \nsimultaneous reception of information and may include other means when s
 uch means are \nnecessary to provide reasonable accommodation to a person 
 with a disability. Public proceedings \nmay not be \nconducted by text-onl
 y means such as e-mail\, text messages or chat functions. \n \nC. Commissi
 oners are expected to be physically present for public proceedings except 
 when being \nphysically present is not practicable. Circumstances in which
  physical presence for one or more \nCommissioners is not practicable may 
 include: \n(1)  The existence of an emergency or urgent issue that require
 s the C\nhttps://www.maine.gov/mhrc/sites/mhrc/files/inline-files/Adopted%
 20MHRC%202021%20Policy%20on%20Remote%20Participation%20in%20Meetings.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/mhrc/sites/mhrc/files/inline-files/Adopted%20MHR
 C%202021%20Policy%20on%20Remote%20Participation%20in%20Meetings.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
