SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 2027 MaineCare Eligibility Changes: Informa
 tion\, Resources\, and Partner Briefing
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			2027 MaineCare Eligibility Changes: Information\, Res
 ources\, and Partner Briefing\n2027 MaineCare Eligibility Changes: Infor
 mation\, Resources\, and Partner Briefing\nAug 21\, 2026\nThe federal gove
 rnment is making changes to MaineCare (Maine’s Medicaid program). These 
 changes apply to Medicaid programs across the country. Last week the O
 ffice of MaineCare Services (OMS) sent out a\nSave-the-Date\nfor an August
  24\, 2026\, partner and provider briefing on upcoming changes to Mai
 neCare eligibility. There is still time to\nregister\n!\nThe Office for F
 amily Independence (OFI) and OMS are working together to implement these
  changes as smoothly as possible to avoid disruptions in coverage for elig
 ible Mainers. Our goal is to provide Mainers with clear\, accurate\, and 
 actionable information so they can confidently understand how these change
 s may affect them.\nWhat is changing?\nAs of January 1\, 2027\, the foll
 owing MaineCare eligibility changes will start:\nFor MaineCare Expansion
  adults:\nNew Work Requirements\; and\nEligibility renewals every
  6 months instead of every 12 months.\nFor all MaineCare members:\nReduc
 tions in retroactive coverage.\nMaineCare Expansion members are adults be
 tween 19 and 64 years old who have MaineCare based on their income. Th
 ey do not meet the\nSocial Security disability guidelines\nor have Medicar
 e.\nWhat can MaineCare Members Do Now?\nThe most important things MaineCar
 e members can do right now are:\nKeep their contact information up to date
  with OFI\,\nRead any letters they receive\,\nContinue renewing their cove
 rage as required\, and\nContinue using their MaineCare benefits.\nWe know
  that members rely on their healthcare providers for trusted information a
 bout MaineCare. We appreciate the value that adds\, as well as the additi
 onal work. Our goal is to support providers through these changes\nResour
 ces to be aware of right now include:\nSave th\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs
 /oms/providers/provider-bulletins/2027-mainecare-eligibility-changes-infor
 mation-resources-and-partner-briefing-2026-08-21
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/2027-maine
 care-eligibility-changes-information-resources-and-partner-briefing-2026-0
 8-21
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
